{"status":"completed","summary":"node1 now has a 1 GiB LUKS2-encrypted XFS volume mounted at /srv/secure. It automatically unlocks and mounts during boot, and persisted data survived the required node restart.","actions_performed":["Installed cryptsetup.","Created a LUKS2 container backed by /var/lib/secure-volume/secure-volume.luks.","Generated a node-local root-only key at /etc/cryptsetup-keys.d/secure_crypt.key.","Configured automatic unlocking in /etc/crypttab and mounting in /etc/fstab.","Verified automatic recovery from a fully closed mapper.","Restarted node1 and confirmed recovery under a new boot identity."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Encrypted volume mounted at /srv/secure","command_ids":["cmd-82b8eaf3b3c044ae","cmd-322184d73e4d4565"],"summary":"The backing file passed LUKS validation; cryptsetup reported an active LUKS2 AES-XTS mapping, mounted as XFS at /srv/secure."},{"requirement":"Automatic unlock and mount at boot","command_ids":["cmd-6e36f68885f44fae","cmd-d66c2b2b2f3f4180","cmd-322184d73e4d4565","cmd-ad61f2325e17446f"],"summary":"crypttab/fstab were configured, the mapper was closed, and starting the generated mount unit automatically restored the mapper, filesystem, and data. The same recovery occurred after reboot."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart and persistence","command_ids":["cmd-e5052452931648c4","cmd-635d110c029e44cb","cmd-d19f32f71c7a44d0","cmd-ad61f2325e17446f"],"summary":"Healthy baseline used boot ID a70d7f83-6867-4c91-851d-7a1228689bb3; reboot was acknowledged; node returned with boot ID a0bd1afe-e6b6-49c0-a4a8-5c4c9f11c4cc; encryption and mount units were active and persisted data remained readable."}]}
